    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36884" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑξάπους</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, ὁ, ἡ, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πουν</span>,
			τό, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδος</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>six-footed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>PA</u>
				683b2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑξάπεδος</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Sat.</u>
				17
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κολοσσός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Luc.</u>
					37
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Milet.</u>
					7.57
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Didyma</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of metre, <i>of six feet,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				4
			</span></i>. Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕξπους.</span></div>
